      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a start but it feels a little too polite for the 50s. i mean, the tension back then wasn't just about \"stirrin' up trouble,\" it was way more visceral and specific. the characters wouldn't be so vague about it. can we make the dialogue a bit more gritty and raw? like, show how they actually feel about the idea of people \"crossing the line\" or mixing in ways they aren't used to. make it feel like a real conversation between two guys who are genuinely worried about their way of life changing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
